IMPORT `chapter-4a-private-defence`

§ `Chapter 15 -- Offences relating to race`

-- Penal Code 1871 ss 298, 298A.
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/PC1871.txt.
--
-- The two live sections of a Chapter that held five; ss 295 to 297, the religion
-- offences, were repealed in 2022 when the Maintenance of Religious Harmony Act took
-- them. s 298 is the deliberate wounding of a person's RACIAL FEELINGS by word,
-- sound, gesture, object or any represented matter. s 298A is PROMOTING ENMITY
-- between racial groups, in two limbs: knowingly promoting disharmony or enmity on
-- grounds of race by words, signs or representations, or committing an act known to
-- be prejudicial to racial harmony which disturbs or is likely to disturb the public
-- tranquility.
--
-- Both are excluded from the s 74 racially-or-religiously-aggravated doubling, being
-- racial offences already, which is why the `Aggravation Facts` record in
-- chapter-3-punishments.l4 names them.
--
-- PUNISHMENT IS NOT COMPUTED.

§§ `Section 298 -- Wounding the racial feelings of a person`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 298"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes uttering words or making gestures with deliberate intent to wound the racial feelings of a person under Penal Code 1871 section 298
GIVEN ro IS A `Racial Offence` @desc With the deliberate intention of wounding a person's racial feelings, uttering a word or sound in his hearing, making a gesture or placing an object in his sight, or causing any matter however represented to be seen or heard by him.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes wounding racial feelings` IF
    ro's `with the deliberate intention of wounding the racial feelings of a person utters any word or makes any sound in the hearing of that person or makes any gesture or places any object in the sight of that person or causes any matter however represented to be seen or heard by that person`

§§ `Section 298A -- Promoting enmity between racial groups`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 298A"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes promoting enmity between racial groups or an act prejudicial to racial harmony under Penal Code 1871 section 298A
GIVEN ro IS A `Racial Offence` @desc Knowingly promoting or attempting to promote, on grounds of race, disharmony or enmity, hatred or ill will between racial groups by words, signs or representations; or committing an act known to be prejudicial to racial harmony which disturbs or is likely to disturb the public tranquility.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes promoting enmity between racial groups` IF
        ro's `by words spoken or written or by signs or by visible representations or otherwise knowingly promotes or attempts to promote on grounds of race disharmony or feelings of enmity hatred or ill will between different racial groups`
    OR  ro's `commits an act which he knows is prejudicial to the maintenance of harmony between different racial groups and which disturbs or is likely to disturb the public tranquility`

§§ `Proposed Act wrappers`

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes a racial offence` IF
        (   `constitutes wounding racial feelings` (a's `racial offence`)
         OR `constitutes promoting enmity between racial groups` (a's `racial offence`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)
